  "result": "Perfect! All 70 tests pass. Here's a summary of what I added:\n\n**Line Discounts Implementation:**\n\n1. **`src/errors.js`** \u2014 Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code for discounts outside 0-100 or non-numeric values.\n\n2. **`src/invoices.js`** \u2014 Updated three functions:\n   - Added `validateDiscountPercent()` helper that validates a discount is a number 0\u2013100 (decimals like 12.5 are allowed), defaults to 0 if undefined\n   - `createInvoice()` now accepts `discountPercent` on each line, validates it, and keeps it on the line object\n   - `addLine()` accepts and validates `discountPercent` for new lines\n   - `invoiceTotals()` now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n     - `subtotal` = sum of all line totals\n     - `discount` = sum of all line discounts (each = `lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100`, rounded with `roundCents()`)\n     - `total` = `Math.max(0, subtotal - discount)` \u2014 clamped at 0 as required\n\n3. **Tests** \u2014 Added 13 new tests covering:\n   - Creating invoices with/without discounts\n   - Decimal discount percentages\n   - Discount validation (outside range, non-numeric)\n   - Totals calculation with discounts\n   - Clamping at 0 when discount exceeds subtotal\n   - Adding lines with discounts\n   - Invalid discount rejection in `addLine()`\n\nAll 70 tests pass \u2713",
